WEBVTT

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:16.160
Polar Bear's Café

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.450
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.990
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:34.350
The Ideal Single Living.

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:38.560
Hey, Mr. Penguin,

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:40.910
don't you think it's perfect for me?

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:43.950
What? Your job at the zoo?

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:45.590
Are you finally taking it seriously?

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:49.140
No, I'm talking about living on my own.

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:50.350
Living on your own?

00:01:50.350 --> 00:01:52.460
What, are you thinking 
about running away again?

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:56.340
Not running away, living on my own.

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:58.240
By myself.

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:59.730
You, Panda? I don't think you're capable.

00:01:58.310 --> 00:01:59.730
By myself.

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:01.260
By myself.

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:01.260
That was a fast reply.

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:03.220
Fast reply <i>(sokutou)</i>?

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:06.680
Manly

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:06.730
That would be a wooden sword <i>(bokutou)</i>.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:09.580
That would be fighting <i>(kakutou)</i>.

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:12.630
Food 
Ticket

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:12.410
That would be a cafeteria <i>(shokudou)</i>.

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:15.190
That would be the hot 
water supply <i>(kyuutou)</i>.

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:17.850
Relaxation must be nice <i>(kyuuyou)</i>.

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:19.700
I'd like to take it easy sometimes.

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.330
Taking it easy is great.

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:25.240
I want to live on my own.

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:27.760
You're always taking it easy.

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:32.780
No, I want to take it easy, 
living on my own.

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:35.210
Living on your own is hard.

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:38.210
You have to do everything on your own.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.720
But that's what's great about it.

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:45.440
Aren't you over glamorizing 
this a bit, Panda?

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:47.430
What kind of lifestyle 
are you thinking about?

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:49.140
You wanna hear?

00:02:49.670 --> 00:02:51.730
On second thought, no, I don't.

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:53.310
Let's see...

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:54.520
You're still going to tell me?

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:56.320
In the morning,

00:02:57.260 --> 00:03:00.340
I'm going to wake up in a huge bed.

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:10.450
Then the curtains will open,

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:20.510
and the skyline of the city
 will spread out before me.

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:22.680
And then, below that,

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:25.600
there will be a whole bamboo thicket.

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:29.600
You need to decide between 
the city or the bamboo thicket.

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:33.270
After I get up, 
I'll be enjoying that view

00:03:35.050 --> 00:03:38.140
while waking up with a 
glass of fresh juice.

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:41.640
Is that juice going to 
be bamboo grass juice?

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:43.540
And then after the bamboo grass juice...

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:44.820
You're going to eat bamboo grass, right?

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:52.190
It looks like everything 
is going to be green.

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:55.090
Or rather, that isn't any different 
from how things are now.

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:57.380
Is there really a reason 
to live on your own?

00:03:57.950 --> 00:03:59.590
And then, listen to this,

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:01.130
I'll hear a knock on the door...

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:09.270
Good morning, Master Panda.

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:10.470
Why me?!

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:13.170
Your schedule for the day is as follows:

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:14.820
Lazing around at 10 A.M.,

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:16.810
having lunch at noon,

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:18.650
lazing around at 1 P.M.,

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:20.850
and lazing around 
after your 3 P.M. snack.

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:22.440
That is all, sir.

00:04:30.140 --> 00:04:32.910
High Class Bamboo Grass Dining

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:35.330
When I get to the restaurant...

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:38.400
Welcome, sir.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:41.260
We have been awaiting your 
arrival, Mr. Panda.

00:04:41.750 --> 00:04:43.760
What?! That's me, too?!

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:55.420
When I get to my table,

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:58.300
there's a grand dinner waiting for me.

00:05:01.690 --> 00:05:04.460
Please enjoy.

00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:12.620
It's all right, I guess.

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:15.830
I don't feel like going to work today.

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:17.940
Could you go in my place?

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:19.360
As you wish, sir.

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:21.090
Why would I go?!

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:24.990
Or rather, that's not really 
living on your own, is it?

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:28.000
This is sounding really fun.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:30.300
I wanna live on my own as soon as possible!

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:33.210
You're not going to 
find a place like that!

00:05:35.690 --> 00:05:36.810
We have that.

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:38.990
What?!

00:05:38.990 --> 00:05:41.860
An ideal place for living 
on your own, right?

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:46.020
It's six tatami mats in size,
 including the closet,

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:48.880
so it's quite large if 
you're living by yourself.

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:50.620
And you can laze around.

00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:56.580
And you can see a bamboo thicket
 through the window.

00:05:57.170 --> 00:06:00.980
I'm looking for something with 
a little more "waaah"

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:03.920
with a bit of "daaah."

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:06.550
A little more "waaah" 
and a bit of "daaah"?

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:09.280
That's way too vague, Panda!

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:10.390
I'm sorry.

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:13.260
We do have a "waaah" 
with a bit of "daaah."

00:06:13.610 --> 00:06:14.760
Really?!

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:16.480
Really?

00:06:20.410 --> 00:06:22.290
This is rather plain.

00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:24.580
It isn't "waaah"?

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:25.950
No, it's not.

00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:27.390
How about "daaah"?

00:06:28.140 --> 00:06:29.320
Not at all.

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:35.940
Your expectations are too high, Panda.

00:06:35.940 --> 00:06:37.720
Nah.

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:43.850
My ideal single living 
house has to be somewhere.

00:06:43.850 --> 00:06:45.690
You sure about that?

00:06:45.690 --> 00:06:49.090
I mean, you're here already, Mr. Penguin.

00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:51.140
I just have to find the 
house to put you in.

00:06:51.140 --> 00:06:54.260
How about we leave me out of 
your ideal living situation?

00:06:56.380 --> 00:06:58.680
It has to exist somewhere.

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:02.150
A bamboo thicket!

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:06.440
Yes! This is my ideal bamboo thicket!

00:07:06.740 --> 00:07:09.480
H-Hey, Panda!

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:12.490
Wow, this is perfect!

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:15.630
It's totally "waaah" 
with a little bit of "daaah"!

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:19.630
I want to live in a place like this!

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:21.100
Huh?

00:07:21.670 --> 00:07:24.670
Um, isn't this your house, Panda?

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:25.660
What?

00:07:26.590 --> 00:07:28.840
Oh. So it is.

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:35.680
I really don't think there's a reason 
for you to move out on your own.

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:39.850
Huh?

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:42.060
Is that you, Badger?

00:07:43.340 --> 00:07:44.970
What are you up to?

00:07:44.970 --> 00:07:46.310
Looking for a place to live?

00:07:46.310 --> 00:07:49.400
Oh, I couldn't stand it anymore.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:50.850
Living on your own?

00:07:51.440 --> 00:07:52.940
It was a big mistake.

00:07:52.940 --> 00:07:56.680
You should be listening to this, Panda.

00:07:56.680 --> 00:07:59.830
Living by yourself isn't all positive.

00:08:00.390 --> 00:08:03.000
I hate the wood flooring in my place.

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:03.920
I want to move out as soon as possible.

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:07.780
Oh, really? 
Isn't it easy to clean?

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:11.310
You should ask Mr. Penguin
 to clean it for you.

00:08:11.310 --> 00:08:13.880
Stop making me a servant!

00:08:15.270 --> 00:08:16.990
Why do you want to move?

00:08:18.410 --> 00:08:19.600
Because...

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:25.600
Holes! I can't dig any 
holes and it's unbearable!

00:08:26.280 --> 00:08:29.570
What? Is it really that rough?

00:08:29.930 --> 00:08:31.770
It'd be about as tough

00:08:31.770 --> 00:08:34.490
as you not being able 
to laze around, Panda.

00:08:35.030 --> 00:08:37.740
Wow, that is rough.

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:42.230
I wonder what kinds of places 
everyone else lives in.

00:08:43.980 --> 00:08:45.120
Welcome!

00:08:45.810 --> 00:08:47.450
Too close, too close. Way too close.

00:08:48.350 --> 00:08:49.840
Here you go.

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:52.190
Please make yourself at home.

00:08:52.190 --> 00:08:54.010
Too close, too close. Way too close...

00:08:56.490 --> 00:08:57.720
Welcome!

00:08:58.390 --> 00:09:01.440
Wow, impressive, Anteater. 
You have your own house?

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:02.880
I splurged and bought one!

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:04.850
With a 35-year loan!

00:09:07.050 --> 00:09:09.280
Please come in and take a look!

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:14.970
This is sort of a sad thought,
but his kids might pay off that loan.

00:09:14.970 --> 00:09:16.780
Considering the average 
lifespan of an anteater...

00:09:17.380 --> 00:09:19.620
Maybe his grandkids.

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:23.950
Oh, it's Mr. Tortoise.

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:26.350
Where are you headed?

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:29.570
To my house...

00:09:29.570 --> 00:09:31.880
Can we come with you?

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:33.920
Show me how it is living on your own.

00:09:34.280 --> 00:09:36.620
Sure...

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:44.490
Wow, this is a really fancy apartment.

00:09:44.490 --> 00:09:45.940
What's the layout?

00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:49.380
2...L...S...

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:51.830
S? What's that?

00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:53.240
A service room?

00:09:53.570 --> 00:09:55.820
No...

00:10:02.030 --> 00:10:04.100
Very glamorous. 
Like a celebrity's apartment.

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:06.000
Does "S" stand for celebrity <i>(serebu)</i>?

00:10:07.570 --> 00:10:10.040
No...

00:10:11.520 --> 00:10:13.960
It's for sand...

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:18.940
This is my ideal... 2LS...

00:10:22.090 --> 00:10:23.390
Coming!

00:10:26.170 --> 00:10:29.140
Oh? What brings you two here?

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:31.300
Thanks for having us over.

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:35.480
Wow, you keep the place pretty clean.

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:37.300
Uh, hey!

00:10:38.340 --> 00:10:40.130
Is this where you drink water?

00:10:40.130 --> 00:10:41.030
That's my bath!

00:10:41.680 --> 00:10:42.530
Then...

00:10:43.100 --> 00:10:45.180
Is this where you drink water?

00:10:45.180 --> 00:10:46.200
That's my toilet!

00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:48.860
I'm impressed, Mr. Handa.

00:10:48.860 --> 00:10:51.630
You keep your bath and 
toilet clean.

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:53.170
Y-Yeah...

00:10:55.780 --> 00:10:58.380
Huh? Is this it?

00:10:58.770 --> 00:11:00.360
This is all of it.

00:11:00.910 --> 00:11:04.100
Well, I guess it's what I'd 
expect from you, Mr. Handa.

00:11:04.960 --> 00:11:06.810
I'll be fine right here.

00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:08.630
What?

00:11:08.630 --> 00:11:10.170
What are you talking about?

00:11:10.170 --> 00:11:12.870
Why don't you sleep 
over there, Mr. Handa?

00:11:13.260 --> 00:11:15.320
What? Why?!

00:11:17.050 --> 00:11:20.180
I'll be putting my things 
on the middle shelf.

00:11:20.580 --> 00:11:23.200
Make sure you don't drink my bamboo 
grass juice without permission.

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:24.520
I won't drink it!

00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:25.950
Or rather, don't put anything in there!

00:11:27.580 --> 00:11:30.180
I want to wake up on my own,

00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:32.500
so please be quiet when 
you leave in the morning.

00:11:32.990 --> 00:11:34.510
I'm telling you, don't sleep there!

00:11:34.510 --> 00:11:36.600
What are you going to do about your job?

00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:40.280
My loyal Mr. Penguin will go instead.

00:11:40.280 --> 00:11:42.760
I told you, stop making me your servant!

00:11:43.380 --> 00:11:46.310
I really want to live on my own,

00:11:46.310 --> 00:11:48.080
but I guess it can't be helped.

00:11:48.080 --> 00:11:50.390
The three of us will manage somehow.

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:52.900
Well then, good night.

00:11:53.530 --> 00:11:56.450
Wake me up when the food is ready.

00:12:01.250 --> 00:12:05.500
So, Mr. Handa said he had to clean 
his bathroom, so you got the boot?

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:07.180
Isn't that rude?

00:12:07.180 --> 00:12:09.870
I can't say that I blame him.

00:12:09.870 --> 00:12:12.790
Do you still want to 
live on your own, Panda?

00:12:14.350 --> 00:12:16.060
I gave up on that.

00:12:16.440 --> 00:12:20.260
Oh! But I did find a servant.

00:12:20.660 --> 00:12:21.540
Right?

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:25.960
Could you give up on me, too?

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:32.810
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:12:29.540 --> 00:12:31.550
Summer Festival!

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:43.490
Polar Bear Style 
Okonomiyaki
 You'll never forget the 
flavor once you try it!

00:12:43.510 --> 00:12:44.950
Super 
Delicious

00:12:43.510 --> 00:12:44.950
Grizzly's 
Yakisoba

00:12:43.510 --> 00:12:44.950
with 
salmon

00:12:45.470 --> 00:12:46.980
Today we're having a collaboration

00:12:46.980 --> 00:12:49.070
between Polar Bear's Café and Grizzly's Bar

00:12:49.070 --> 00:12:50.700
and running a food stand!

00:12:51.040 --> 00:12:52.250
Sounds great.

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:53.720
I can't wait!

00:12:53.720 --> 00:12:55.370
That looks good on you, Miss Sasako.

00:12:55.680 --> 00:12:57.840
Let's all do our best!

00:12:57.840 --> 00:12:59.250
Okay!

00:12:59.970 --> 00:13:01.980
Leave the festival to me!

00:13:01.980 --> 00:13:03.850
I'll burn it up!

00:13:03.850 --> 00:13:05.880
So cool!

00:13:05.910 --> 00:13:09.050
Fool

00:13:06.370 --> 00:13:09.140
Please make the yakisoba, Grizzly.

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:10.390
Hell yeah!

00:13:10.390 --> 00:13:11.890
I'll make tons!

00:13:12.260 --> 00:13:15.230
You're in charge of applying 
the sauces and such, Panda.

00:13:15.610 --> 00:13:16.850
Leave it to me!

00:13:17.300 --> 00:13:19.480
You'll be in charge of gathering 
the crowd, Mr. Penguin.

00:13:19.480 --> 00:13:20.830
Roger!

00:13:20.830 --> 00:13:21.850
Um...

00:13:23.550 --> 00:13:26.030
is there anything I can help with?

00:13:26.440 --> 00:13:28.940
Oh, it's been a while!

00:13:28.940 --> 00:13:30.860
Is he a friend of yours, Panda?

00:13:30.860 --> 00:13:32.950
Yeah! He's my older brother!

00:13:33.320 --> 00:13:34.980
Older brother?

00:13:34.980 --> 00:13:36.170
Or something like that...

00:13:36.450 --> 00:13:38.630
What's your relationship?

00:13:38.990 --> 00:13:41.180
He's a relative that has the same name

00:13:41.180 --> 00:13:43.050
but is from a different family.

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:44.550
Huh?

00:13:45.120 --> 00:13:49.010
We were the ones that were 
originally called pandas.

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:51.720
Wow, really?

00:13:52.300 --> 00:13:55.710
But since the appearance of giant pandas,

00:13:55.710 --> 00:14:01.030
we started being called lesser pandas.

00:14:01.690 --> 00:14:03.030
Wow.

00:14:03.950 --> 00:14:06.640
We still exchange information 
about bamboo grass

00:14:06.640 --> 00:14:09.590
and get together for family gatherings.

00:14:09.590 --> 00:14:11.080
Information on bamboo grass?

00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:15.400
Yes. Like finding the best 
places for bamboo grass.

00:14:15.400 --> 00:14:19.250
We like bamboo grass, too, 
so we try to work together.

00:14:19.600 --> 00:14:21.430
Wow.

00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:26.270
Then I'll be waiting on customers and taking orders,

00:14:26.270 --> 00:14:28.800
so could we ask you to ring people up?

00:14:29.280 --> 00:14:30.260
Sure!

00:14:32.190 --> 00:14:34.050
Wow, awesome!

00:14:34.770 --> 00:14:35.990
This is the one I want!

00:14:37.730 --> 00:14:40.270
Oh, yeah. I should put this out.

00:14:40.290 --> 00:14:41.520
Happy Hour

00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:43.650
Happy hour?

00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:45.670
What kind of special are you offering?

00:14:45.670 --> 00:14:48.050
Extra portions? Lower prices?

00:14:48.050 --> 00:14:49.320
Nothing, really.

00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:50.280
What?

00:14:50.630 --> 00:14:52.530
But if people see this sign,

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:54.700
people will think they should buy it now!

00:14:55.160 --> 00:14:57.000
Play fair, damn it!

00:14:57.000 --> 00:15:07.010
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:09.240
Come and get it! Come and get it!

00:15:09.240 --> 00:15:13.390
We've got Polar Bear style 
okonomiyaki and Grizzly yakisoba!

00:15:13.900 --> 00:15:16.750
Once you eat it, you'll never forget it!

00:15:16.750 --> 00:15:19.420
Not to mention, you rarely
 get the chance to eat them.

00:15:26.040 --> 00:15:28.780
Damn it. This is too slow!

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:32.760
Yeah!

00:15:32.760 --> 00:15:34.580
Take that and that and that!

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:38.200
Be astounded by the deliciousness 
of Grizzly yakisoba!

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:43.310
Take that and that!

00:15:44.180 --> 00:15:47.090
You're too enthusiastic, Grizzly.

00:15:47.390 --> 00:15:48.840
I want two yakisoba!

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:51.420
I want one okonomiyaki and one yakisoba!

00:15:51.420 --> 00:15:52.720
Right away!

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:55.410
Can I get three yakisoba and 
one okonomiyaki, please!

00:15:55.410 --> 00:15:57.060
Can you make modern yaki?

00:15:57.060 --> 00:15:58.680
Yes, we can!

00:16:00.360 --> 00:16:03.910
Please hurry with the okonomiyaki, Panda!

00:16:03.910 --> 00:16:06.320
Oh, right... Right away!

00:16:08.580 --> 00:16:10.820
I just got sauce on myself.

00:16:11.170 --> 00:16:12.970
Come on! Hurry up!

00:16:12.970 --> 00:16:14.070
O-Okay.

00:16:16.420 --> 00:16:17.140
There.

00:16:17.930 --> 00:16:19.260
What the hell are you doing?

00:16:20.150 --> 00:16:21.500
It was backwards.

00:16:30.190 --> 00:16:31.880
Change with Sasako, damn it!

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:38.890
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:16:38.890 --> 00:16:40.640
Here you go.

00:16:40.930 --> 00:16:42.220
Yay!

00:16:42.220 --> 00:16:43.820
Good for you.

00:16:43.820 --> 00:16:45.860
Thank you very much.

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:49.440
Sold Out 
Thank You Very Much

00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:48.180
We're sold out!

00:16:48.180 --> 00:16:49.440
We can close up shop now.

00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:51.610
Thank you all for your hard work.

00:16:52.650 --> 00:16:53.990
Thanks.

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:55.140
Thanks, everyone.

00:16:55.640 --> 00:16:57.770
Wow, I'm beat!

00:16:57.770 --> 00:17:00.130
Working is so hard!

00:17:00.130 --> 00:17:02.990
You got fired partway through,
 remember, Panda?

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:05.400
Let's go around to the other stands.

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:07.420
Oh, good idea.

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:11.880
Wow! There're so many!

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:14.630
I'm gonna get this one!

00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:17.660
Panda in panda.

00:17:17.660 --> 00:17:19.260
That's really weird.

00:17:19.540 --> 00:17:20.970
Then...

00:17:21.280 --> 00:17:23.410
Panda and panda.

00:17:23.830 --> 00:17:25.500
That's scary.

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:36.490
Cotton Candy
White 100 yen
Pink 200 yen
Blue 300 yen

00:17:28.040 --> 00:17:31.140
Wow! That looks fun! I wanna try!

00:17:31.140 --> 00:17:33.570
Don't be so troublesome.

00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:35.660
Oh, do you want to try?

00:17:36.750 --> 00:17:38.200
I do! I do!

00:17:49.950 --> 00:17:52.750
You've turned into a completely 
different creature.

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:56.470
My tongue won't reach!

00:18:00.370 --> 00:18:01.470
Bamboo Caramel

00:18:01.450 --> 00:18:03.500
Aw, so close!

00:18:03.500 --> 00:18:05.910
One more time! One more time!

00:18:09.170 --> 00:18:10.680
Oh, hey...

00:18:10.680 --> 00:18:14.280
This gun doesn't work. 
Can I get another one?

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:16.200
Stop being such a nuisance.

00:18:21.940 --> 00:18:23.080
I did it!

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:23.750
Look!

00:18:23.750 --> 00:18:24.620
Let me see that.

00:18:25.090 --> 00:18:26.080
Take that!

00:18:28.330 --> 00:18:29.620
Did you see that?

00:18:29.620 --> 00:18:31.460
That's what happens 
when you mess with me!

00:18:32.460 --> 00:18:33.550
Here you go.

00:18:34.540 --> 00:18:37.320
Th-Thank you.

00:18:47.650 --> 00:18:50.130
They're too damn small!

00:18:50.130 --> 00:18:52.600
I'd get them in one swipe if they 
were salmon or trout!

00:18:52.600 --> 00:18:54.650
You're amazing, Mr. Polar Bear!

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:57.210
That's your 20th one!

00:18:57.210 --> 00:18:58.740
Good job.

00:19:02.020 --> 00:19:04.170
How about I handle this more personally?

00:19:04.170 --> 00:19:06.750
Sir, please don't...

00:19:10.860 --> 00:19:12.930
Oh, Mr. Handa.

00:19:12.930 --> 00:19:14.910
Oh, hey, Panda.

00:19:14.910 --> 00:19:17.510
I just finished work and got here.

00:19:17.910 --> 00:19:20.660
Where's Miss Sasak— I mean, the stand?

00:19:20.660 --> 00:19:24.110
Oh, we sold out, 
so everyone's off having fun.

00:19:24.440 --> 00:19:26.300
Oh, I see.

00:19:26.300 --> 00:19:28.090
What's that?

00:19:28.090 --> 00:19:32.330
Oh, this is for Miss Sasako— I mean,
for everyone to share.

00:19:32.330 --> 00:19:34.210
Some tea and some juice.

00:19:34.210 --> 00:19:36.700
Miss Sasako is right over there.

00:19:36.700 --> 00:19:38.940
Huh? Oh, I see.

00:19:39.540 --> 00:19:41.160
Let's go give them to her.

00:19:41.160 --> 00:19:41.700
What?!

00:19:42.160 --> 00:19:45.830
I think just the two of you 
should drink them together.

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:47.530
No, um, uh...

00:19:47.530 --> 00:19:49.870
Oh, Mr. Handa.

00:19:50.260 --> 00:19:52.540
M-Miss Sasako.

00:19:52.540 --> 00:19:53.790
Good evening.

00:19:55.300 --> 00:19:58.070
H-H-Hello.

00:19:58.070 --> 00:20:00.790
Mr. Handa brought us something.

00:20:00.790 --> 00:20:02.630
H-Here.

00:20:02.630 --> 00:20:05.120
Oh, thank you very much.

00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:08.150
Oh, it's not much.

00:20:08.150 --> 00:20:09.520
Hey, Panda...

00:20:10.050 --> 00:20:12.770
Thanks, Handa. I'll gladly take it.

00:20:15.760 --> 00:20:17.690
I'll have one, too!

00:20:18.570 --> 00:20:20.190
I'll have one, as well.

00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:23.270
Well, since you offered, I'll take one.

00:20:23.580 --> 00:20:25.620
Oh, yes. Please help yourselves.

00:20:25.650 --> 00:20:27.610
Hey, do you have any alcohol?

00:20:26.150 --> 00:20:29.360
Mr. Handa just can't catch a break.

00:20:27.610 --> 00:20:29.310
How about seal meat?

00:20:29.310 --> 00:20:31.870
I'm sorry. I didn't bring any...

00:20:35.610 --> 00:20:37.630
Oh, fireworks!

00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:39.520
Looks like they started.

00:20:42.420 --> 00:20:45.050
Wow, they're so pretty!

00:20:45.710 --> 00:20:48.100
I love fireworks.

00:20:49.680 --> 00:20:52.780
Me, too. I love them, too.

00:20:54.400 --> 00:20:56.850
Fireworks are so amazing.

00:20:58.150 --> 00:20:59.040
Sure are.

00:21:04.490 --> 00:21:06.780
Please have a seat, Miss Sasako.

00:21:06.780 --> 00:21:08.200
Oh, thank you.

00:21:12.500 --> 00:21:15.690
Come on, Mr. Handa. Don't hold back.

00:21:16.480 --> 00:21:19.810
But now you were able to sit together.

00:21:32.020 --> 00:21:36.400
Th-This is the last one,

00:21:36.400 --> 00:21:37.790
but please have some tea.

00:21:37.790 --> 00:21:39.760
Thank you very much!

00:21:39.760 --> 00:21:41.730
I'm rather thirsty.

00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:45.340
It's so nice and cold.

00:21:57.380 --> 00:21:58.750
So pretty!

00:22:00.390 --> 00:22:02.250
Burn it up! Burn it up!

00:22:02.420 --> 00:22:05.810
Wrong thing, Grizzly.

00:22:05.810 --> 00:22:06.970
They're sparkling!

00:22:07.590 --> 00:22:11.980
Jeez, you guys are so dense.

00:23:54.970 --> 00:24:24.520
Next Time

00:23:58.270 --> 00:23:59.660
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:59.660 --> 00:24:00.620
What?

00:24:00.620 --> 00:24:03.060
Can I spread a rumor 
that whoever says your name

00:24:03.060 --> 00:24:04.920
ten times will be cursed?

00:24:05.230 --> 00:24:06.180
No.

00:24:06.180 --> 00:24:08.550
If it was that easy to curse 
someone, I'd be way too busy.

00:24:08.550 --> 00:24:11.230
Then could you tell us 
 the non-stingy way

00:24:11.230 --> 00:24:15.180
of saying "splitting the 
check" that you came up with?

00:24:15.180 --> 00:24:17.100
I don't think we should 
discuss that at the beach.

00:24:17.100 --> 00:24:18.100
Or rather, let's end this.

00:24:18.100 --> 00:24:19.840
Next week's Polar Bear's Café

00:24:19.840 --> 00:24:21.190
will be presented at breakneck speed.

00:24:21.190 --> 00:24:22.610
Let's do it slow and steady.

00:24:21.600 --> 00:24:24.520
Panda Is No Longer A Panda

00:24:22.610 --> 00:24:24.020
Enjoy!
